From 466e38fa4f62765c9a1191bb89a5f6ad130adc08 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: leo <leoschlosser@tutamail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 17:07:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] misc: add Samsung modem_if for the Note II's XMM6262, enable
 it on n710x

Port of Samsung's modem_if (drivers/misc/modem_if of the Galaxy S III/Note II
3.0 kernels), reduced to the configuration of the GT-N7100: Intel/Infineon
XMM6262 3G modem on the Exynos4412's HSIC0 port, SIPC4 framing, runtime L2
link PM over the HOST_WAKEUP/SLAVE_WAKEUP handshake. The userspace interface
is kept, so Samsung's boot daemon (cbd) and RIL run unchanged:
/dev/umts_boot0, umts_ipc0, umts_rfs0, umts_csd, umts_router, umts_ramdump0,
umts_loopback0, multipdp, /dev/link_pm, rmnet0-2 and
/sys/devices/platform/s5p-ehci/ehci_power (forwarded to the exynos-ehci
ehci_power hack).

Changes against Samsung's code: GPIOs from the device tree (board-m0-modems.c
folded into modem_main.c), Android wakelocks mapped onto wakeup sources, no
AP panic on a CP crash dump request, NULL ops guarded, current kernel APIs.

The modem needs the PMIC's 32 kHz CP clock: the boot ROM loads PSI/EBL and
the firmware without it, but the firmware then hangs (PHONE_ACTIVE high,
never enumerates as 1519:0020). Stock left the clock on from the bootloader;
mainline gates it as unused, so the modem node takes it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
